WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:22.500
OSHA 10 is not optional. You need this to work on most commercial job sites.

00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:45.000
Confined space entry, excavation safety, scaffolding, and ladder safety.
Permit-required confined spaces have limited entry/exit and may contain
hazardous atmospheres. HVAC technicians encounter confined spaces in mechanical

00:00:45.000 --> 00:01:07.500
Here are the key terms. Write these down.

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:30.000
Confined Space: Space with limited entry/exit that may contain hazardous
atmospheres. Requires permit and atmospheric testing.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:52.500
Competent Person: OSHA-defined person capable of identifying hazards and
authorized to take corrective action.

00:01:52.500 --> 00:02:15.000
Here's why this matters on the job: Confined space incidents are often fatal.
Never enter without proper procedures and atmospheric testing.

00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:37.500
Watch out for these: Test atmosphere before entering any confined space. And —
Never enter alone

00:02:37.500 --> 00:03:00.000
Take a minute before you move on. What's the one thing from this lesson you need
